<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93555" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σειρᾱφόρος</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σειρηφ-</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵππος</span>), a horse
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>which draws by the trace
				only</i> (being harnessed by the side of the pair under the
			yoke, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ζύγιοι</span>),
			<i>trace-horse</i>: hence metaph., sts. <i>yoke-mate,
			coadjutor</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				842
			</span></i>; sts. <i>one who has light work</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				1640
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				1300
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. [κάμηλος</span>] <i>attached
				like a trace-horse</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.102
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>carrying a lasso</i>, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σειρά</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1.3
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
